    [Refactor][310P] Avoid bool-mask IndexPut in GDN prefill state init (#19295)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    In the 310P GDN prefill path, `_forward_core` uses two indexed
    assignments on
    the recurrent state for every layer. On Ascend both of them lower to the
    generic IndexPut implementation, which is pure operator overhead in this
    layer;
    the boolean-mask form additionally has to convert the mask into an index
    tensor before writing.
    
    This PR replaces both with equivalent dedicated operators:
    
    - Clearing the initial state of requests without history:
      `initial_state[~has_initial_state, ...] = 0` -> `masked_fill_` with a
    broadcast mask. One element-wise kernel, no mask-to-index
    materialization,
      and exactly the same positions are cleared.
    - Writing the final recurrent state back to the paged cache:
      `ssm_state[indices] = ...` -> `index_copy_` on a flattened 2D view. A
    dedicated single-dimension copy instead of the generic multi-dimensional
      IndexPut template, writing the same rows to the same slots.
    
    Both changes are bit-exact: the indices are unique per request, no
    accumulate
    path is involved, and the dtype conversion and arithmetic are unchanged.
    There
    is no API or behavior change outside this layer.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No. The change only replaces how the 310P GDN prefill path clears and
    writes
    back its recurrent state internally. The results are bit-exact, and
    there is no
    change to public APIs, configuration options, kernel signatures, or the
    behaviour of any non-310P backend.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Accuracy: served Qwen3.5 on Atlas 300I Duo with both the baseline
    build and
    this patch, and compared the generated outputs over the same prompts;
    the
      results are identical.
    
    - Profiling: collected a MindStudio trace of a prefill step and
    confirmed the
      two indexed assignments no longer take the generic IndexPut path.
    
